<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>body{font:10px DejaVu Sans,sans-serif}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}th,td{padding:6px;border:1px solid #ddd;text-align:left;overflow-wrap:break-word}th{background:#f4f4f4}</style></head><body><h1>Canteen report</h1><p>{{ $from }} to {{ $to }} &middot; {{ $data['group_by']==='order'?'Detailed orders':'Grouped by '.$data['group_by'] }}</p><p>Non-cancelled orders: {{ $data['summary']['orders'] }} &middot; Total value: Rs {{ number_format($data['summary']['gross'],2) }} &middot; Company contribution: Rs {{ number_format($data['summary']['company_share'],2) }} &middot; Employee contribution: Rs {{ number_format($data['summary']['employee_share'],2) }}</p>@if($data['group_by']==='order')<p>Each row is one separate order. Cancelled orders have zero payable amounts and are excluded from summary totals. Item/category filters show only matching products and contributions.</p>@elseif($data['group_by']==='employee')<p>Total units = total quantity of the product. Number of orders = separate orders containing that product. The summary counts each order once.</p>@endif<table><thead><tr>@foreach($table[0] as $heading)<th>{{ $heading }}</th>@endforeach</tr></thead><tbody>@foreach(array_slice($table,1) as $row)<tr>@foreach($row as $cell)<td>{{ $cell }}</td>@endforeach</tr>@endforeach</tbody></table></body></html>